#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139313} :activity/id #uuid "34c94a44-5f76-59c0-84d9-7b40675893b6" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050170 :topic/id #uuid "33c13e3d-3762-500d-989e-3f05f79647a4" :topic/math-academy-id 2321} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139313 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139702 :tutorial/content "To evaluate a power, we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the resulting product.\n\nSo, to find the value of $9^2$, we first write it out with multiplication signs as follows:\n$2$\n\nThen, we compute the product:\n\n$$\n9^{2} = 9 \\cdot 9 = 81\n$$\n\nRaising a number to the power of $2$ is known as **squaring** a number. Therefore, the following are equivalent.\n\n- $9^2 = 81$\n- The **square** of $9$ is $81$.\n- $9$ raised to the *second* power equals $81$." :tutorial/id #uuid "c1b4655c-0ae1-50ce-a37f-b3d77fdc30d7" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8587 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "c0f28c5d-f43b-501f-8bff-e540fd9f4ed1" :step/math-academy-id 174935 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139314}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139314 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138401 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138135 :question/id #uuid "b5313725-78fc-57ee-9acc-19d03f6624bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-13752"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c336cc3-c89e-5af2-b170-1fc6d9cf8307" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048285}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138712} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138861}] :knowledge-point/title "Squaring a Number"} :step/id #uuid "a8a467bd-8210-5b7a-b178-dbc650740db0" :step/math-academy-id 174936 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139315}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139315 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139743 :tutorial/content "Let's evaluate the following exponent:\n\n$$\n2^{\\color{red}{3}}\n$$\n\nWe start by writing our exponent as repeated multiplication:\n$3$\n\nNow, we compute the product.\n\nSince\n\n$$\n2 \\times 2 = 4\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 \\cdot 2_(⏟)_(4) \\cdot 2 &= 4 \\cdot 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{4}}\\times 2=8\n$$\n\nwe have $2^3=8$.\n\nRaising a number to the power of $3$ is known as **cubing** a number. Therefore, the following are equivalent.\n\n- $2^3 = 8$\n- The **cube** of $2$ is $8$.\n- $2$ raised to the *third* power equals $8$." :tutorial/id #uuid "2cf5f36c-da57-5e4b-91e8-76c86e67837f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9457 :tutorial/title "The Cube of a Number"} :step/id #uuid "dcb4b4ef-c7f3-590f-b3b4-e20adba6c4f6" :step/math-academy-id 174940 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139316}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139316 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138402 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138136 :question/id #uuid "213a088d-3427-5313-adc2-1fcc9d64bb74" :question/math-academy-id "e-13754"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc1a0e6d-ed51-5797-8ab7-305e861d1109" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050735}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138713} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138759}] :knowledge-point/title "Cubing a Number"} :step/id #uuid "a90baf5a-9d3a-5ef4-badb-989c18ead40c" :step/math-academy-id 174941 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139317}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139317 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138403 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138137 :question/id #uuid "0c0e05b6-e633-5b9e-a070-3e26e0349355" :question/math-academy-id "e-13757"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2cd9435f-cb8b-57b2-99ce-d856f613b0fd" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138758} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139173}] :knowledge-point/title "Raising a Number to the First Power"} :step/id #uuid "b741f0f4-7d97-5992-8675-c44f666b1b9f" :step/math-academy-id 174944 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139318}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186139318 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138404 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138138 :question/id #uuid "d4e63087-a01f-59b3-bf6c-cf7cbfa3ce78" :question/math-academy-id "e-13760"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "70a364f5-5384-5ba6-8142-5740aa51f4bc" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138714} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138923}] :knowledge-point/title "Raising Zero or One to a Power"} :step/id #uuid "a3261c23-f926-5ca7-ab3c-8a935b0af579" :step/math-academy-id 174947}] :activity/title "Evaluating Exponents" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186138624}]}
